  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone and KB through a series of target interactions. This compound is implicated in targeting Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which in turn is a target of Isodaucene and Yuanhunine, both of which ultimately direct their targets to KB. The shared pathway highlights a possible mechanism where 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone may influence KB via a mitochondrial thioredoxin-dependent pathway. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, indicating a plausible, though not yet fully characterized, mechanism by which 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone could interact with KB. The integration of these targets suggests a broader role in cellular processes, potentially involving redox regulation or metabolic pathways, which could be further explored to elucidate the precise molecular mechanism.",
